  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat percentage increase occurs when the campus population doubles in one month? The number of students on campus triples at the end of every month. There are 12 students on campus at the beginning of the year. Percentage increase is calculated relative to the original population.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The original population is \\(12\\) students. If it doubles, the new population is\n\n\\[\n2(12)=24.\n\\]\n\nThe increase is\n\n\\[\n24-12=12.\n\\]\n\nThus, the percentage increase relative to the original population is\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{12}\\times 100\\%=100\\%.\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{100\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. The number of students on campus doubles at the end of every month.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Initially, there are \\(12\\) students. Since the population doubles at the end of the month:\n\n\\[\n12 \\times 2 = 24\n\\]\n\nThe increase is\n\n\\[\n24-12=12\n\\]\n\nUsing the original population as the reference:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{12}\\times 100\\%=100\\%\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the percentage increase is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{100\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. There are 10 students on campus at the beginning of the year.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The original population is \\(10\\) students. After doubling:\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 2 = 20\n\\]\n\nThe increase is:\n\n\\[\n20-10=10\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the percentage increase is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{10}\\times 100\\%=100\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{100\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Oh, I forgot to mention: the student population is multiplied by 2 after each completed month.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The initial population is \\(10\\) students. After one completed month, it is multiplied by \\(2\\):\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 2 = 20.\n\\]\n\nThe increase is:\n\n\\[\n20-10=10.\n\\]\n\nRelative to the original population, the percentage increase is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{10}\\times 100\\%=100\\%.\n\\]\n\nThus, after one month, the population has increased by\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{100\\%}.\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many students will be on campus after three completed months?",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Starting with \\(10\\) students and multiplying by \\(2\\) after each completed month:\n\n- After 1 month: \\(10 \\times 2=20\\)\n- After 2 months: \\(20 \\times 2=40\\)\n- After 3 months: \\(40 \\times 2=80\\)\n\nEquivalently,\n\n\\[\n10\\cdot 2^3=80.\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{80\\text{ students}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: A doubling means the new population is twice the original population.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "A doubling means multiplying the current population by \\(2\\). Starting with \\(10\\) students:\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 2^3 = 10 \\times 8 = 80.\n\\]\n\nSo after three completed months, there will be\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{80\\text{ students}}.\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "GOOD: —\nBAD: —\nWATCH: \"I should also tell you: A doubling means\"",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How many additional students would have joined campus by the end of May beyond the students present at the beginning of the year? One more thing you should know: the question concerns the number of students on campus by the end of May.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "There are \\(5\\) completed months from the beginning of the year through the end of May. Thus,\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 2^5 = 320\n\\]\n\nstudents are on campus by the end of May.\n\nThe number of additional students is\n\n\\[\n320-10=310.\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{310\\text{ additional students}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
